                               (Destinations.kt L55, /digital-twin); wired in
                               TeslaSyncApplication.onCreate() (NavHost registration).

SI BOUNDARY (P1/S5)
  This surface carries no displayed SI quantity: the physical-state fields are booleans / enums
  (door/window/lock/sentry/charge-port/seat/lights). The charging-active predicate reads the SI
  canonical `charger_power_w` (with the legacy `charger_power_kw` as a fallback during the SI
  migration) but renders only the boolean "Charging" / "Yes"; nothing is stored converted. The only
  render-boundary formatting is the locale-aware last-updated time (web `useDateFormat.formatTime`).

LIVE DATA / STALENESS (ADR-013)
  None of the four feeds is an SSE live stream; each is a cache-then-network Resource stream
  projected to UiState (the web page polls every 5s via refetchInterval — the native refresh()
  trigger is the analogue), so the header DataFreshness chip surfaces fetchedAt / refreshing /
  stale / error. The reused VehicleTwin / VehicleSelect surfaces carry their own freshness tiers.

